{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790696144,"nonce":"Fy7O2Kh6WikhNpgYAunCBp1vx4o=","title":"Package the Future ABI for upstream HashLink users","message":"Generated Promise operations return ash.Future\u003cT\u003e, and xgpu.hdll resolves the matching hlp_future_* symbols from its host. Ash supplies both pieces, but a program launched by upstream HashLink does not currently have a documented, installable package that guarantees the Haxe class and native ABI symbols are present.\n\nDefine and ship that dependency as part of the hlwgpu installation story. The haxelib metadata and release archive should make the requirement resolvable without cloning Ash or building Rust tooling, and a stock HashLink smoke test should request an adapter, await a device, and observe both Future resolution and rejection.","files":null}]}